  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The metatarsals are a set of five long bones in the foot, positioned between
    the tarsal bones and the phalanges of the toes. They are numbered I to V, starting
    medially (big toe side) to laterally (little toe side):

    Metatarsal I: Associated
    with the big toe, it''s the thickest and shortest.

    Metatarsal II: Slightly
    longer than the first, it plays a key role in walking and balancing.

    Metatarsal
    III: Aligns with the center of the foot.

    Metatarsal IV: One of the mid-length
    metatarsals, near the outer edge of the foot.

    Metatarsal V: Corresponds
    to the little toe and has a tuberosity at its base, often a site for bunionette
    formation.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
