  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The supraspinous fossa is a concave depression located on the dorsal aspect
    of the scapula, superior to its prominent spine. This fossa is bounded by the
    medial and lateral borders of the scapula and the spine itself. It serves as
    the origin site for the supraspinatus muscle, one of the four rotator cuff muscles
    crucial for stabilizing and moving the shoulder joint. The supraspinatus muscle
    emerges from this fossa and passes under the acromion to attach to the greater
    tubercle of the humerus. The shape and integrity of the supraspinous fossa are
    significant in assessing shoulder health and function.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
