      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The lower teeth are a set of structures rooted in the alveolar process
    of the mandible, functioning in mastication and aiding in speech. Typically,
    an adult has 16 lower teeth: 4 incisors, 2 canines, 4 premolars, and 6 molars
    (including 2 third molars, often referred to as wisdom teeth). These teeth vary
    in shape and size, each tailored for specific roles in biting, tearing, or grinding
    food. Dental health is vital not only for efficient digestion but also for preventing
    conditions like gum disease or tooth decay. Issues with the lower teeth can affect
    speech, chewing, and overall oral health, making regular dental care essential.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
