      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The vomer is a slender, flat bone situated in the midsagittal plane of
    the skull. It forms the posterior part of the nasal septum, dividing the nasal
    cavity into left and right halves. The upper surface of the vomer connects with
    the sphenoid and ethmoid bones, while its lower part articulates with the maxilla
    and palatine bones. Its primary role is structural, contributing to the partition
    of the nasal passages. Abnormalities or fractures of the vomer can lead to nasal
    septum deviations, affecting airflow and possibly requiring medical correction.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
