      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Teeth are hard, calcified structures located in the jaws, essential for
    mastication (chewing) and speech articulation. In humans, teeth are classified
    by their function and location:\r\nIncisors (8 total): These are the central
    and lateral teeth in the front of the mouth, characterized by their flat, chisel-shaped
    crowns. They are crucial for biting and cutting food.\r\nCanines (4 total): Also
    known as cuspids, these are pointed and situated next to the incisors. \nPremolars
    (8 total): Located after the canines, they have two or more cusps. \nMolars (12
    total, including wisdom teeth): Situated in the back of the mouth, molars have
    broad and flat surfaces, making them ideal for grinding and crushing food."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
