  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The skull frontal bone, also known simply as the frontal bone, is one
    of the major bones that make up the human skull. It is situated at the front
    of the cranium and forms the forehead region, as well as the roof of the eye
    sockets (or orbits). The frontal bone extends from the area above the eyes to
    the top of the head, where it meets the parietal bones.\r\n\r\nAn important feature
    of the frontal bone is the frontal sinus, which is a hollow, air-filled cavity
    located within the bone. The frontal sinus is one of the paranasal sinuses and
    is responsible for producing mucus, which helps to moisten and filter the air
    we breathe.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
