  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Also known as the jugular or suprasternal notch, the sternal notch is a
    distinct, central indentation located on the superior border of the manubrium
    of the sternum. Situated between the clavicular notches, this depression is easily
    palpable at the base of the neck, and it serves as an important anatomical landmark
    for clinical examinations and certain medical procedures. The sternal notch aids
    in orienting medical professionals to the level of the fourth thoracic vertebra
    and is also used as a reference point in assessing the trachea's position, among
    other structures.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
