  m_text: "An important feature of the frontal bone is the frontal sinus, which is
    a hollow, air-filled cavity located within the bone. The frontal sinus is one
    of the paranasal sinuses and is responsible for producing mucus, which helps
    to moisten and filter the air we breathe.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
