      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Ribs are curved, elongated bones originating from the vertebral column
    and extending anteriorly toward the thoracic wall. In humans, there are typically
    12 pairs of ribs, classifying them as:



    True Ribs (1-7): Directly attached
    to the sternum via costal cartilages, these ribs provide protection to vital
    organs like the heart and lungs.


    False Ribs (8-10): While they do have
    costal cartilages, these don''t connect directly to the sternum but instead to
    the cartilage of the rib above.


    Floating Ribs (11-12): These are short
    ribs that do not attach to the sternum at all.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
