      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The superior angle of the scapula refers to the point where the medial
    (or vertebral) border meets the superior border of the bone. This angle is located
    roughly at the level of the second thoracic vertebra. Its orientation is significant
    for anatomical reference and is particularly noteworthy in postural assessments.
    The superior angle provides an attachment site for the levator scapulae muscle,
    a muscle vital for elevating the scapula and tilting its glenoid cavity inferiorly. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
